My mom's cake business has a real website now, live on the internet, and I built it.
She was taking cake orders through the phone. So there was no way for people 
to see flavors or prices without texting her number. 

Now that I have set up her website, people can see her flavors, prices, quote forms, 
and a gallery of her past work all in one place. 

Before setting up my mother's website, I wanted to make sure I could build
a working automation that I could add to it. While setting up a workflow on my own, 
I ran into a few obstacles. For example, I made a node which sends a form's user data to a 
google sheet. When I was setting up my google account's credentials in n8n, Brave started blocking 
the sign in popup. I thought the credentials I typed in were wrong. But then I found that Brave doesn't 
tell you when it blocks the popup, it lets the sign in disappear and it makes you wonder 
if your login's broken. When I went to check, I found the google sign in right away. 
Lesson: check for a blocked popup before you assume your credentials are wrong.

Another obstacle I ran into was when I almost sent a confirmation email to a stranger. 
I was testing an auto reply node and looked back at the "To" field before running it. 
I saw that it wasn't my test email at all. I also saw that the node was pulling from Google 
Sheets instead of from my webhook, and Sheets had some old test rows in it from earlier runs. 
It took one of those instead of my submission. I already like to check the outputs before hitting 
execute, and here I caught that there would've been a real person getting a random "thanks for your 
order" email.

Now that I have a live site running for my mother, 
I am going to add a working automation on top of it 
that gets quote requests straight to her phone. 
I already plan to make one for my father's courier company too.
